// @probe reject: is a method on the value, not a free function
// `clamp(15, 0, 10)` lowered to `self.clamp(15, 0)`, so rustc reported that the agent struct is
// not `Ord`. It is method-only like the string builtins, but valid on a number, so it needs its
// own list: the one that rejects a scalar receiver would have rejected the correct spelling too.
agent Main { public void Run() { print clamp(15, 0, 10); } }
